(4610395, 661425, 17203, '<td valign="top">I can''t really see any significant cloning marks and dm21384 didn''t contact SC or request validation on the entry. Cloning is legal in advanced... as long as you don''t clone out visually prominent parts of the original. I thought it was a strong entry, and it''s a shame it had to be DQ''d. :-(</td>', 'I can''t really see any significant cloning marks and dm21384 didn''t contact SC or request validation on the entry. Cloning is legal in advanced... as long as you don''t clone out visually prominent parts of the original. I thought it was a strong entry, and it''s a shame it had to be DQ''d. :-(', '2008-04-03 10:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610689, 661425, 14476, '<td valign="top">Again, with the greatest respect for the SC, this is another<br/>example of why the use of the "one size fits all" Disqualification<br/>Details information simply does not say adequately <b>why</b> the<br/>image was DQed. <br/> <br/>we cannot learn from perceived mistakes if we don''t know what<br/>the maker may have done incorrectly.</td>', 'Again, with the greatest respect for the SC, this is anotherexample of why the use of the "one size fits all" DisqualificationDetails information simply does not say adequately why theimage was DQed.  we cannot learn from perceived mistakes if we don''t know whatthe maker may have done incorrectly.', '2008-04-03 12:03:05.000000', NULL, 0),
