(4612775, 661425, 66192, '<td valign="top">This is an area of DPchallenge that kills me. The rule on this topic is so vague and leaves the interpretation up to the site council. if you look at Scalverts entry as an example,  he cloned out fishing line, which is sort of the same thing here isnt it?</td>', 'This is an area of DPchallenge that kills me. The rule on this topic is so vague and leaves the interpretation up to the site council. if you look at Scalverts entry as an example,  he cloned out fishing line, which is sort of the same thing here isnt it?', '2008-04-04 05:38:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612838, 661505, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by The Puppetmaster:</b></div><hr/><i>The peeps wouldn''t stand up on that either, so I snipped their little butts off with scissors to expose the sticky marshmallow inside (ha). </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Don''t even try to claim that no peeps were harmed in the making of this photo. I may have done some things to woodies - torn limbs off, burned them, submerged them in hot oil, carved faces in them with a dremel tool, BUT I NEVER snipped their little butts off. There oughta be a law...<br/> <br/>:P<br/> <br/>A little late congrats, by the way. Much patience, much effort, nice reward.</td>', 'Originally posted by The Puppetmaster:The peeps wouldn''t stand up on that either, so I snipped their little butts off with scissors to expose the sticky marshmallow inside (ha).  Don''t even try to claim that no peeps were harmed in the making of this photo. I may have done some things to woodies - torn limbs off, burned them, submerged them in hot oil, carved faces in them with a dremel tool, BUT I NEVER snipped their little butts off. There oughta be a law... :P A little late congrats, by the way. Much patience, much effort, nice reward.', '2008-04-04 06:04:55.000000', NULL, 0),
